            <ArticleTitle>[Continuous peridural morphine analgesia in refractory pain in urology].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>280-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Peridural catheterization connected to a sub-cutaneous morphine reservoir can provide an effective and prolonged analgesia for certain pelvic pains of a urological origin which resist the usual sedative therapies. The authors describe the method of catheterization and the results which they have obtained in five patients treated in this way.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
